# Mobile App API Contract — Feature: User Authentication and Authorization

## Overview
This document defines the REST API contracts for the user authentication and authorization feature. It specifies HTTP methods, request/response structures, authentication requirements, and the data models used by the mobile application and the backend service. All endpoints are designed to be idempotent and secure.

## Authentication Endpoints

### GET /auth/token

Request: `POST /auth/token`  
Body: `{"user_id": "uid123", "password": "pass123"}`

Response:
```json
{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
  "refresh_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 1800,
  "user_id": "uid123",
  "user_name": "John Doe",
  "roles": ["user"],
  "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:23:45Z"
}
```

Request Validation:
- `user_id` must be a non-empty string.
- `password` must be at least 8 characters and contain at least one uppercase letter.

### POST /auth/logout

Request: `POST /auth/logout`  
Headers: `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`

Response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "User logged out successfully"
}
```

## Authorization Endpoints

### GET /auth/me

Request: `GET /auth/me`  
Headers: `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`

Response:
```json
{
  "user_id": "uid123",
  "user_name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "roles": ["user"],
  "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:23:45Z"
}
```

### GET /auth/permissions

Request: `GET /auth/permissions`  
Headers: `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`

Response:
```json
{
  "user_id": "uid123",
  "permissions": [
    {
      "scope": "read-user",
      "resource": "user",
      "action": "read",
      "description": "View user profile"
    },
    {
      "scope": "manage-user",
      "resource": "user",
      "action": "read",
      "description": "View user details"
    },
    {
      "scope": "manage-user",
      "resource": "user",
      "action": "update",
      "description": "Update user details"
    },
    {
      "scope": "manage-user",
      "resource": "user",
      "action": "delete",
      "description": "Delete user account"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Error Responses

All errors return a standardized structure:

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "AUTH-001",
    "message": "Invalid credentials",
    "details": {
      "user_id": "uid123"
    },
    "type": "AuthenticationError",
    "http_status": 401
  },
  "user": {
    "user_id": "uid123",
    "user_name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john.doe@example.com",
    "roles": ["user"]
  }
}
```

HTTP Status Codes:
- 400 — Bad Request
- 401 — Unauthorized
- 403 — Forbidden
- 404 — Not Found
- 500 — Internal Server Error
- 503 — Service Unavailable

## Data Models

### Authentication Token

```csharp
public class AuthenticationToken
{
    public string AccessToken { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string RefreshToken { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string TokenType { get; set; } = "Bearer";
    public int ExpiresIn { get; set; }
    public string UserId { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string UserName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public List<string> Roles { get; set; } = new();
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
}
```

### User Entity

```csharp
public class User
{
    public Guid UserId { get; set; }
    public string UserName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Email { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string PasswordHash { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Role { get; set; } = "user";
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public List<UserPermission> Permissions { get; set; } = new();
}
```

### User Permission

```csharp
public class UserPermission
{
    public Guid PermissionId { get; set; }
    public string Scope { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Resource { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Action { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
}
```

## Mobile Implementation Notes

- The mobile app should use a short-lived access token and a refresh token to avoid repeated authentication requests.
- Refresh tokens are stored securely in the device’s secure storage and should be rejected if accessed after expiration.
- Permission requests should not be cached across sessions. Each session should verify permissions independently.
- All responses must include a `user` object for backward compatibility with older clients.
- Error response formatting should remain consistent across mobile and web clients.

## Acceptance Criteria

- The mobile app can log in with valid credentials and receive an access and refresh token.
- The app can refresh the access token without re-authenticating.
- Logged-out and unauthorized requests return a 401 response.
- The app can request and verify permissions for the authenticated user.
- All responses follow the defined error format and HTTP status codes.
- The API remains idempotent for login and logout operations.
